  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1129 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nAfter the front finally clears the region on Thursday night,\nthings return to seasonable normals through the weekend.\nNondescript surface patterns and zonal flow aloft put temperatures\nright around normal (90 degrees) with heat indices just barely \napproaching 100. However, the extended forecast for next week does\nlook to heat up some more. Warm fronts lifting over the area in \nconjunction with upper level ridging spell out another hot period \nfor Middle TN starting on Monday. Too early to make any calls\nright now but we may be flirting with Heat Advisory criteria again\nas early as Tuesday of next week.",
